meta {
    title: "DocUP Phase 1 — Full Feature Test",
    author: "Prathmesh",
    version: "1.0.0"
}

h(1) { DocUP Phase 1 }
h(2, id: "intro", class: "section") { Introduction }

p {
    DocUP is a document markup language with b{single-pass parsing},
    i{zero ambiguity}, and explicit scoping. This paragraph shows
    b{bold}, i{italic}, b{i{bold italic}}, and inline code{let x = 1;}
    all in one place.
}

hr {}

h(2, id: "links") { Links and Quotes }

p {
    Learn more at link("https://example.com") { the DocUP homepage },
    or read the link("https://example.com/spec", title: "Spec") { language spec }.
}

quote {
    Good design is as little design as possible.
}

hr {}

h(2, id: "lists") { Lists }

p { An unordered list of core features: }
list {
    item { Metadata blocks for document info }
    item { Headings from h(1) through h(6) }
    item { Paragraphs with b{bold}, i{italic}, and code{inline code} }
}

p { An ordered list of build steps: }
list(ordered: true) {
    item { Lex the source into tokens }
    item { Parse tokens into an AST }
    item { Analyze the AST for errors }
    item { Generate the final HTML }
}

hr {}

h(2, id: "media") { Images and Code }

image("https://example.com/diagram.png", alt: "Architecture diagram")

codeblock(lang: "go", file: "main.go") {!
package main

import "fmt"

func main() {
    fmt.Println("Closing brace } and quotes \" work fine!")
}
!}

p {
    That's all 10 Phase 1 features: meta, headings, paragraphs, inline
    styling, codeblock, hr, list/item, link, quote, and image.
}
